  "body": "## Summary\nOwner directive 2026-08-15: add real Part3+4 GTM-certification completion tracking to `pm-sentinel-tick.sh` (min tokens, real audit, real completion certificate). `pm.md` / desktop-sentinel `SKILL.md` were already updated separately (prose, no PR needed) -- this is the code-level equivalent for this repo (task-20260815-114156).\n\n## What changed\n- **New `gtm_part34_certification_check.py`**: one real round-trip that live-queries `gtm_certification_categories` for OCID-020 (never a hardcoded count/list -- the SPEC's own illustrative \"9 gap rows\" was already stale by dispatch time; live-verified 7 real gap rows as of 2026-08-15). Only when genuinely 0 gap rows AND every `passed=1` row carries real non-placeholder evidence AND no prior certificate already exists (idempotent -- no per-tick audit-log spam) does it write ONE real, timestamped, evidence-citing completion record -- reusing the **existing** `ocid_master_standard_audit_log` table via `record_ocid_master_standard_audit_event()` (same convention `gtm_write_category_result.py` already established for this table), never a new table.\n- **New Check 4 in `pm-sentinel-tick.sh`**: calls the above once per tick. On a real gap, does a real content-based in-flight search (`resource_governor.py --query-umr --search`) ahead of dispatch -- necessary because the known seed UMRs (UMR-20260815-033344-4799 / UMR-20260815-042226-f271, both verified live as `status=failed`, not in-flight) were dispatched by a different mechanism, so this script's own STATE_FILE dedup layer alone can't see them or any real successor redispatch. If genuinely not in flight, dispatches exactly one real `pm_lifecycle.py`-driven fix through the file's existing `dispatch_gap()`/`DISPATCH_OWNER_TASK_SH` gateway (tier 1, repo=compliance-tracker) -- same single-gateway, no-bypass discipline every other check in this file already follows.\n\n## Verification (real, not fabricated)\n- Live-queried the real DB directly before building: 25 total rows, 7 real gap rows (not the SPEC's \"9\" -- confirms the SPEC's own warning that the count would drift).\n- Live-queried both seed UMRs: both `status=failed`.\n- Live `--search` for the gap content: 20 matches, all `completed`/`rejected_duplicate` -- nothing in flight right now.\n- `bash -n pm-sentinel-tick.sh` -- syntax OK.\n- `python3 -m py_compile` + `pyflakes gtm_part34_certification_check.py` -- clean.\n- 3 new pytest fixtures added to `test_pm_sentinel_tick.py` (9-gap dispatch path, 0-gap-all-evidenced certify path incl. idempotency, already-in-flight no-op path), run for real: **`pytest test_pm_sentinel_tick.py -v` -> 14 passed** (11 pre-existing + 3 new), 51.37s, zero failures.\n\nFull verification detail: `progress/task-20260815-114156-pm-in-server--add-real-part3-4-gtm-cert.md`.\n\nNever self-certified -- requesting a real independent AUDIT:PASS before merge, per this repo's Rule 10 / mandatory-audit-check convention.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
